[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Main Line"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "positional,solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "pawn-chain,defend-d4,b3-break"]
[Kind "main"]

1. e4 e6 2. d4 { Builds a big centre. The d4 pawn will be the base of our pawn chain, so most of this opening is about keeping it safe. }
2... d5 3. e5 { Gains space and shuts Black's light-squared bishop in behind its own e6 pawn. Black must now attack our pawn chain. }
3... c5 4. c3 { Puts a pawn behind d4, because Black's c5 pawn already attacks it. }
4... Nc6 5. Nf3 { Develops and adds another guard to d4, which the c5 pawn and the knight on c6 both attack. [%cal Gf3d4,Rc5d4,Rc6d4] }
5... Qb6 { The queen adds a third attacker on d4 and also eyes b2. } 6. a3 { A calm move that stops ...Bb4+ and prepares b4. The bishop stays on c1, where it guards b2 from the queen. }
6... c4 { Black grabs space and stops our bishop going to d3. }
( 6... cxd4 7. cxd4 { Recapture with the pawn so the centre stays ours. } 7... Nge7 8. Nc3 { Another guard for d4 and a piece developed. } )
( 6... Bd7 7. b4 { Challenges the c5 pawn at once, before Black can lock the queenside with ...c4. } 7... cxd4 8. cxd4 Rc8 9. Bb2 { Now the bishop has a free diagonal and still guards our queenside. } )
7. Nbd2 { Develops the knight that is not needed on c3, so the c3 pawn keeps backing up d4. It also prepares b3 to attack the c4 pawn. }
7... Na5 { Black's knight protects c4 and watches b3. }
( 7... f6 8. Be2 { Black hits the e5 pawn. We simply develop and trade when it is safe. } 8... fxe5 9. Nxe5 { Takes back with the knight, which is safe on e5 because Nxe5 dxe5 recaptures. } )
8. Be2 { The bishop cannot use d3, since the c4 pawn covers it, so it goes to e2 and gets ready to castle. }
8... Bd7 9. O-O { Castle now so the king is safe before the centre opens up. }
9... Ne7 10. Rb1 { The rook leaves a1 to support the b-pawn, which will push to b4 or b3 to break up Black's queenside. }
10... h6 11. Re1 { Plan: keep d4 guarded, then hit the c4 pawn with b3 and bring the knights round, for example Nf1-g3, to attack the king. If Black leaves the book, count the defenders of d4 and b2 before every move. } *
